Most Asked DevOps Interview Question at MNCs
 
Q: Why do we use two COPY commands in a Dockerfile instead of one?
 
❌ Bad approach:
COPY . .
RUN pip install -r requirements.txt
 
✅ Good approach:
COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install -r requirements.txt
COPY . .
 
The answer: Docker Layer Caching.
 
Every line in a Dockerfile creates a layer.
If a layer hasn't changed, Docker reuses it from cache.
 
With single COPY → you change one line in app.py → pip install runs again (2-3 minutes wasted every build).
 
With two COPYs → requirements.txt didn't change → pip install is cached → only app code rebuilds.
 
Build time drops from minutes to seconds.
 
Rule of thumb: Things that change LEAST go at the TOP. Things that change MOST go at the BOTTOM.
 
This is one of the most commonly asked questions in DevOps interviews across MNCs and product companies. 
